Well, my first 3.4.3 Ascension is Lloran the Elven Ranger.  I started him in
December to allow myself some respite from the shift-z/e/hack/repeat of
Smith-A my extinctionist.  Genoless and polyless were the only conducts I
considered for this game.  My notes were pretty sparse, so here's the
highlights of what happened



According to my logfile he was the 6th in a series of elven rangers, the
best of whom made it to level 8 of the dungeon previously.  I found the
bones of two of the others along the way, one in the mines, and the other on
the oracle level.



Lloran was lucky in three ways: first, that the bones elves hadn't used too
many of their arrows.  Second, that he found the bones of a hearsed rogue at
minetown with the +3 grimtooth in it.  That made saving my arrows till the
all important ?oEW were found and blessed.  And lastly that !oFH were Smoky,
leading to a long lived pet Djinn and two wishes while alchemizing just
before the Sanctum.



Minesend had a wheeze when I spotted a silver dragon (polytrap) but a
poisoned arrow arrow killed it in the first volley, The scales were a
welcome change from the mithril.



I ended up with well over 100 elven arrows that I worked up to +7, poisoned
and then fireproofed.  I had meant to do that on my bow, but forgot to
re-weild it after enchanting the arrows.  I guess I was confused as well as
Lloran.  I used my starting bow until the castle when I found some more ?oEW
and got the longbow enchanted up.



Ghennom was boring, but not as boring as my extinctionst standing in the
mess on level 2 summoning monsters.  I switched out grimtooth for a silver
dagger along the way, which I enchanted up.  I killed Rodney, took the book
down to the VS and levelported back to my stash chest on level 6.  I
alchemized 22 !oFH and blessed them and the 5 found ones.  Drank the 22 and
bagged the rest.  Got two djinn wishes along the way,  2 markers.  Wrote
some ?oCharging and the 4 ?oGD



The secret door was on the top of the sanctum room, making it nigh
impossible to line moloch's favorite up from outside.  I ended up wasting a
/oDeath charge to avoid that potential wide angle beam from moloch.  I just
got one lightning bolt for my trouble.  The c!oGL was well used here.



Rodney and the mysterious force were not too much trouble, 7 returns from
the wiz and 8 throwbacks from the force.  The Elemental planes were Easy, I
dodged most of the elementals on air (they can't see invisible?)  The portal
on Fire was 10 moves from the entry, never seen it that close.  Even water
only took about 200 turns to float the bubble to the portal.



Astral was another story!  I had to use 3 of my !oFH over the course of the
plane.  OMG, I had Famine coming out of center branch, so I headed away from
him after killing the 4 master liches that dogpiled on the elf and his
angel.  The summoned nasties were a pain, especially the 3 master mind
flayers. The guardian angel of mars went down fast.  I was machine gunning
arrows any time I had a chance, and poking things with my sliver dagger
otherwise.  Pesty harassed me, eating the /oD every time he got too close.
His branch was Lawful.  I worked my way back, noticing that Famine had
backed up his branch, I headed that way, running into an Archon who wouldn't
close to melee range, just kept blinding and stunning me.  I finally put on
my blindfold and with a final burst of arrows, made it into the altar room.
The High altar of Chaos was a welcome sight, I asked the priest for the
obligatory two bits and then offered Mars his bauble.



